{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "alert-linter",
          "version": "dev",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "invalid-rule",
              "name": "InvalidRule",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Rule file or rule cannot be parsed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A rule that Prometheus cannot load never fires. Broken YAML or PromQL usually means a whole group is silently missing until someone notices the gap during an incident."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A rule that Prometheus cannot load never fires. Broken YAML or PromQL usually means a whole group is silently missing until someone notices the gap during an incident.",
                "markdown": "**Rule file or rule cannot be parsed**\n\nA rule that Prometheus cannot load never fires. Broken YAML or PromQL usually means a whole group is silently missing until someone notices the gap during an incident."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#invalid-rule",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "paging-missing-for",
              "name": "PagingMissingFor",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Paging alert has no `for:` duration"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Without `for:` the alert fires on the first evaluation where the expression is true. One slow scrape, a restart or a deploy blip is enough to wake someone, and the alert resolves before they open a laptop. Requiring the condition to persist is the cheapest way to remove pages nobody can act on."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Without `for:` the alert fires on the first evaluation where the expression is true. One slow scrape, a restart or a deploy blip is enough to wake someone, and the alert resolves before they open a laptop. Requiring the condition to persist is the cheapest way to remove pages nobody can act on.",
                "markdown": "**Paging alert has no `for:` duration**\n\nWithout `for:` the alert fires on the first evaluation where the expression is true. One slow scrape, a restart or a deploy blip is enough to wake someone, and the alert resolves before they open a laptop. Requiring the condition to persist is the cheapest way to remove pages nobody can act on."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#paging-missing-for",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "short-for",
              "name": "ShortFor",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`for:` is shorter than the configured minimum"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A `for:` shorter than an evaluation interval or two barely debounces anything: the alert flaps between firing and resolved, each flap can notify, and responders learn that the alert is noise."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A `for:` shorter than an evaluation interval or two barely debounces anything: the alert flaps between firing and resolved, each flap can notify, and responders learn that the alert is noise.",
                "markdown": "**`for:` is shorter than the configured minimum**\n\nA `for:` shorter than an evaluation interval or two barely debounces anything: the alert flaps between firing and resolved, each flap can notify, and responders learn that the alert is noise."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#short-for",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-runbook-url",
              "name": "MissingRunbookUrl",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No `runbook_url` annotation (or it is not a URL)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "At 03:00 the responder needs to know what to check first and how to mitigate. A runbook link turns a page into a procedure and is the difference between a five-minute and a fifty-minute response. Error on paging alerts, warning otherwise."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "At 03:00 the responder needs to know what to check first and how to mitigate. A runbook link turns a page into a procedure and is the difference between a five-minute and a fifty-minute response. Error on paging alerts, warning otherwise.",
                "markdown": "**No `runbook_url` annotation (or it is not a URL)**\n\nAt 03:00 the responder needs to know what to check first and how to mitigate. A runbook link turns a page into a procedure and is the difference between a five-minute and a fifty-minute response. Error on paging alerts, warning otherwise."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#missing-runbook-url",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-summary",
              "name": "MissingSummary",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No `summary` annotation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The summary is the notification title in most pagers and chat tools. Without it the responder sees only an alert name and must open a dashboard to learn what is wrong and where. Error on paging alerts, warning otherwise."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The summary is the notification title in most pagers and chat tools. Without it the responder sees only an alert name and must open a dashboard to learn what is wrong and where. Error on paging alerts, warning otherwise.",
                "markdown": "**No `summary` annotation**\n\nThe summary is the notification title in most pagers and chat tools. Without it the responder sees only an alert name and must open a dashboard to learn what is wrong and where. Error on paging alerts, warning otherwise."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#missing-summary",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-description",
              "name": "MissingDescription",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No `description` annotation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The description carries the context a summary cannot: what the threshold means, user impact and the likely blast radius. It helps the responder decide quickly whether to escalate."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The description carries the context a summary cannot: what the threshold means, user impact and the likely blast radius. It helps the responder decide quickly whether to escalate.",
                "markdown": "**No `description` annotation**\n\nThe description carries the context a summary cannot: what the threshold means, user impact and the likely blast radius. It helps the responder decide quickly whether to escalate."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#missing-description",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-severity",
              "name": "MissingSeverity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No severity label"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Routing decides who gets woken up from the severity label. An alert without one either falls through to a default receiver nobody watches or pages by accident."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Routing decides who gets woken up from the severity label. An alert without one either falls through to a default receiver nobody watches or pages by accident.",
                "markdown": "**No severity label**\n\nRouting decides who gets woken up from the severity label. An alert without one either falls through to a default receiver nobody watches or pages by accident."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#missing-severity",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unknown-severity",
              "name": "UnknownSeverity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Severity value is not in the allowed list"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Values such as `crit`, `P1` or `High` slip past Alertmanager routes that match on exact values, so the alert silently goes to the wrong place or nowhere."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Values such as `crit`, `P1` or `High` slip past Alertmanager routes that match on exact values, so the alert silently goes to the wrong place or nowhere.",
                "markdown": "**Severity value is not in the allowed list**\n\nValues such as `crit`, `P1` or `High` slip past Alertmanager routes that match on exact values, so the alert silently goes to the wrong place or nowhere."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#unknown-severity",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-owner-label",
              "name": "MissingOwnerLabel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No team/owner label"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An alert without an owner pages whoever holds the default route. Ownership labels let routing reach the team that can actually fix the problem and make alert-quality reviews possible per team."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An alert without an owner pages whoever holds the default route. Ownership labels let routing reach the team that can actually fix the problem and make alert-quality reviews possible per team.",
                "markdown": "**No team/owner label**\n\nAn alert without an owner pages whoever holds the default route. Ownership labels let routing reach the team that can actually fix the problem and make alert-quality reviews possible per team."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#missing-owner-label",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "cause-based-paging",
              "name": "CauseBasedPaging",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Paging alert fires on a resource cause (CPU, memory, disk)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "High CPU or memory is a cause, not a symptom: plenty of healthy systems run hot, and plenty of outages happen at 20% CPU. Paging on causes produces pages with no user impact and misses outages that do have it. Page on symptoms users feel (errors, latency, SLO burn rate) and send causes to a ticket or dashboard."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "High CPU or memory is a cause, not a symptom: plenty of healthy systems run hot, and plenty of outages happen at 20% CPU. Paging on causes produces pages with no user impact and misses outages that do have it. Page on symptoms users feel (errors, latency, SLO burn rate) and send causes to a ticket or dashboard.",
                "markdown": "**Paging alert fires on a resource cause (CPU, memory, disk)**\n\nHigh CPU or memory is a cause, not a symptom: plenty of healthy systems run hot, and plenty of outages happen at 20% CPU. Paging on causes produces pages with no user impact and misses outages that do have it. Page on symptoms users feel (errors, latency, SLO burn rate) and send causes to a ticket or dashboard."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#cause-based-paging",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "rate-window-too-short",
              "name": "RateWindowTooShort",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rate()/increase() window shorter than N x scrape interval"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rate() needs at least two samples inside its window. With a window under about four scrape intervals, one missed or late scrape leaves too few samples, the expression returns nothing and the alert cannot fire, exactly when the target is struggling."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "rate() needs at least two samples inside its window. With a window under about four scrape intervals, one missed or late scrape leaves too few samples, the expression returns nothing and the alert cannot fire, exactly when the target is struggling.",
                "markdown": "**rate()/increase() window shorter than N x scrape interval**\n\nrate() needs at least two samples inside its window. With a window under about four scrape intervals, one missed or late scrape leaves too few samples, the expression returns nothing and the alert cannot fire, exactly when the target is struggling."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#rate-window-too-short",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "high-cardinality-grouping",
              "name": "HighCardinalityGrouping",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Paging alert aggregates by a high-cardinality label"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`sum by (pod)` on a paging alert turns one incident into one page per pod. A bad rollout across 40 pods should be one page with 40 pods in the description, not 40 pages. Warning only, because some per-instance pages are deliberate."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "`sum by (pod)` on a paging alert turns one incident into one page per pod. A bad rollout across 40 pods should be one page with 40 pods in the description, not 40 pages. Warning only, because some per-instance pages are deliberate.",
                "markdown": "**Paging alert aggregates by a high-cardinality label**\n\n`sum by (pod)` on a paging alert turns one incident into one page per pod. A bad rollout across 40 pods should be one page with 40 pods in the description, not 40 pages. Warning only, because some per-instance pages are deliberate."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#high-cardinality-grouping",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "duplicate-alert",
              "name": "DuplicateAlert",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Same alert name and identical labels defined twice"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Two definitions with the same identity look like one alert to Alertmanager. Silences, inhibitions and grouping hit both, and responders see duplicate or flip-flopping notifications for what is really a copy-paste mistake."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Two definitions with the same identity look like one alert to Alertmanager. Silences, inhibitions and grouping hit both, and responders see duplicate or flip-flopping notifications for what is really a copy-paste mistake.",
                "markdown": "**Same alert name and identical labels defined twice**\n\nTwo definitions with the same identity look like one alert to Alertmanager. Silences, inhibitions and grouping hit both, and responders see duplicate or flip-flopping notifications for what is really a copy-paste mistake."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#duplicate-alert",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unknown-directive",
              "name": "UnknownDirective",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Inline directive names a rule that does not exist"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A misspelt disable comment does nothing, so the finding it was meant to silence keeps failing CI and people learn to ignore the linter."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A misspelt disable comment does nothing, so the finding it was meant to silence keeps failing CI and people learn to ignore the linter.",
                "markdown": "**Inline directive names a rule that does not exist**\n\nA misspelt disable comment does nothing, so the finding it was meant to silence keeps failing CI and people learn to ignore the linter."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/mohammed-saaduddin-ansari/alert-linter#unknown-directive",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "prometheus",
                  "alerting",
                  "on-call"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "paging-missing-for",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "paging alert \"HostHighCPU\" (severity=critical) has no `for:`, so one bad evaluation pages someone. Suggestion: add `for: 5m` (or whatever the condition needs to be meaningful) so it must persist before anyone is woken"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "examples/bad-rules.yaml",
